(Title) Tj
T*
(Primary Care Psychological Intervention for Post-ICU Trauma Symptoms: Protocol for a) Tj
T*
(Randomized Clinical Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Intensive care unit survivors frequently experience posttraumatic stress) Tj
T*
(symptoms affecting quality of life, yet few interventions are tested in primary care) Tj
T*
(settings. This protocol describes a randomized evaluation of a brief psychologically-) Tj
T*
(informed intervention delivered by general practitioners. Methods: We will randomize) Tj
T*
(approximately 310 adult ICU survivors with clinically significant PTSD symptoms to receive) Tj
T*
(either a brief exposure-based intervention delivered by their primary care physician \(4-6) Tj
T*
(sessions over 3 months\) or enhanced usual care consisting of regular primary care plus) Tj
T*
(psychoeducational materials. Participants will be identified through ICU discharge records) Tj
T*
(and contacted for screening. Primary outcomes measure health-related quality of life at 6) Tj
T*
(and 12 months using standardized instruments. Secondary outcomes include PTSD symptom) Tj
T*
(severity, anxiety, depression, and functional outcomes. Mediation analyses will examine) Tj
T*
(whether improvements in PTSD symptoms explain quality-of-life gains. Participants will) Tj
T*
(provide questionnaire data at baseline, 3 months, 6 months, and 12 months. This pragmatic) Tj
T*
(trial will evaluate implementation feasibility and cost-effectiveness of primary-care-) Tj
T*
(based mental health intervention.) Tj
ET
